<div id="laserheightprobe_tab" class="laserheightprobe lhp">

  <div class="lhp-brand">
    <img src="plugin/laserheightprobe/static/img/octoburn-128.png" alt="OctoBurn">
    <div>
      <div class="lhp-brand-name">OctoBurn</div>
      <div class="lhp-brand-tag">Laser burns that land where you drew them: focus, surfaces, rotary, camera and LightBurn.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- the status strip: what is fitted and what can fire, on every pane -->
  <div class="lhp-head">
    <div class="lhp-chips" data-bind="foreach: uiChips">
      <span data-bind="css: $parent.uiChipCss(level), attr: {title: title || ''}">
        <i data-bind="css: icon"></i>
        <span class="lhp-chip-label" data-bind="text: label"></span>
        <span class="lhp-chip-value" data-bind="text: value"></span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn-mini lhp-detect" data-bind="click: detect, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()"
            title="Ask the printer what is fitted (M1006, M114, the laser's safety state)"><i class="fas fa-sync-alt"></i> Detect</button>
  </div>

  <!-- the safety bar: armed, running, waiting for a tap, failed -->
  <div class="lhp-bar lhp-bar-armed" data-bind="visible: uiArmed">
    <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
    <strong data-bind="text: uiArmedText"></strong>
    <span class="lhp-bar-note">LightBurn's burns fire.</span>
    <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: uiDisarm"><i class="fas fa-power-off"></i> Disarm</button>
  </div>
  <div class="lhp-bar lhp-bar-run" data-bind="visible: running() && !waitingForTap()">
    <i class="fas fa-cog fa-spin"></i>
    <strong data-bind="text: uiRunTitle"></strong>
    <span class="lhp-bar-note" data-bind="text: message"></span>
    <div class="progress lhp-progress" data-bind="visible: total() > 0">
      <div class="bar" data-bind="style: {width: percent() + '%'}"></div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: abort"><i class="fas fa-stop"></i> Stop</button>
  </div>
  <div class="lhp-bar lhp-bar-tap" data-bind="visible: waitingForTap">
    <i class="fas fa-hand-point-up"></i>
    <strong>Tap the probe pin with a finger now.</strong>
    <span class="lhp-bar-note">Push the deployed pin up gently. The job starts when the probe feels it, and gives up after 60 s.</span>
    <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: abort"><i class="fas fa-stop"></i> Stop</button>
  </div>
  <div class="alert alert-error lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: error">
    <i class="fas fa-times-circle"></i> <span data-bind="text: error"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="alert alert-error lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: settingsError">
    <i class="fas fa-cog"></i> <strong>The settings are not safe to use:</strong> <span data-bind="text: settingsError"></span>
  </div>

  <!-- a 3D print head is back on, or the laser needs ThermalRunaway off -->
  <!-- ko ifnot: isLaser -->
  <div class="lhp-card lhp-card-center" data-bind="visible: headSwapReady">
    <i class="fas fa-cube lhp-big-icon"></i>
    <h4>No laser fitted</h4>
    <p class="muted">The printer reports <span data-bind="text: detectedText"></span>. Heating and 3D prints are allowed, so the laser tools are hidden.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="alert alert-error lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: !headSwapReady()">
    <h4><i class="fas fa-ban"></i> Not ready to 3D print</h4>
    <p data-bind="text: headSwapText"></p>
    <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: readyToPrint, enable: canProbe() && printerReady()">Get ready to 3D print</button>
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <!-- ko if: isLaser -->
  <div class="alert lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: headSwapInfo().thermal === 'enabled'">
    <i class="fas fa-thermometer-half"></i>
    ThermalRunaway is on. With the laser fitted the bed reads about -14 C, and it would stop the printer.
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: readyForLaser, enable: canProbe() && printerReady()">Set up for the laser</button>
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <div class="alert alert-info lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: headSwapInfo().restart">
    <i class="fas fa-redo"></i> Restart OctoPrint (System menu, Restart OctoPrint) to apply the ThermalRunaway change.
  </div>
  <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: headSwapMessage, visible: headSwapMessage"></p>

  <div class="alert lhp-alert" data-bind="visible: isLaser() && detectedWarning() && uiProbeOnline() && !uiArmed()">
    <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
    <strong>The probe is connected.</strong> Never fire with the probe in the bay: park the laser beam-down on something that
    cannot burn. The laser refuses to fire unless it is seated on the head.
  </div>
  <!-- ko if: isLaser -->
  <ul class="nav nav-pills lhp-nav" data-bind="foreach: uiTabs">
    <li data-bind="css: {active: $parent.uiActive() === id}">
      <a href="#" data-bind="click: function () { $parent.uiSelect(id); }"><i data-bind="css: icon"></i> <span data-bind="text: label"></span></a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <!-- /ko -->

  <!-- ===================================================================== BURN -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('burn')">

    <div class="lhp-card lhp-ready" data-bind="visible: uiReady().length, css: {'lhp-card-ok': uiReadyBad() === 0, 'lhp-card-danger': uiReadyBad() > 0}">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-clipboard-check"></i> Ready to burn <span class="lhp-ready-sum" data-bind="text: uiReadySummary"></span></h5>
      <ul class="lhp-checks" data-bind="foreach: uiReady">
        <li data-bind="css: 'lhp-check-' + level">
          <i data-bind="css: $parent.uiCheckIcon(level)"></i>
          <span data-bind="text: text"></span>
          <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="visible: fix && $parent.uiFixLabel(fix), click: function () { $parent.uiFix(fix); }, text: $parent.uiFixLabel(fix)"></button>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-link"></i> LightBurn</h5>
      <p class="lhp-lead" data-bind="text: bridgeText"></p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: bridge().enabled">
        LightBurn connects as a GRBL laser over TCP (port 2323). Pick a mode here, then frame and start from LightBurn.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- flat bed -->
    <!-- ko ifnot: rotaryOn -->
    <div class="lhp-card" data-bind="visible: bridge().enabled">
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">1</span> Focus</h5>
      <label class="radio lhp-choice">
        <input type="radio" name="lhp_focus" value="bed" data-bind="checked: uiFocusMode">
        On the bed, or on material
        <input type="number" step="0.1" min="0" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: uiFocusHeight, enable: uiFocusMode() === 'bed'"> mm thick
      </label>
      <label class="radio lhp-choice">
        <input type="radio" name="lhp_focus" value="here" data-bind="checked: uiFocusMode">
        From the last Probe here <span class="muted">(Control tab panel)</span>
      </label>
      <label class="radio lhp-choice" data-bind="visible: uiHasCamera">
        <input type="radio" name="lhp_focus" value="frame" data-bind="checked: uiFocusMode">
        At the last Frame from LightBurn <span class="muted">(the red dot measures its centre)</span>
      </label>
      <label class="radio lhp-choice" data-bind="visible: uiHasCamera">
        <input type="radio" name="lhp_focus" value="dot" data-bind="checked: uiFocusMode">
        From the red dot, at the box drawn on the Camera tab
      </label>
      <label class="checkbox lhp-choice lhp-auto" data-bind="visible: uiHasCamera, attr: {title: 'In flat mode with the laser not armed: each Frame from LightBurn is measured with the red dot and the focus set there, before you press Start'}">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: uiAutoFrame, click: uiSetAutoFrame, enable: canProbe">
        Focus automatically after each Frame
      </label>
      <p class="lhp-preview" data-bind="text: uiFocusPreview().text, css: {'text-error': uiFocusPreview().bad}"></p>

      <h5><span class="lhp-step">2</span> Flat mode <span class="lhp-auto-note" data-bind="text: uiAutoNote"></span></h5>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: function () { uiFlatStart(false); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && !dotBusy() && !uiFocusPreview().bad"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> <span data-bind="text: bridge().mode === 'flat' ? 'Apply this focus' : 'Flat mode'"></span></button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { uiFlatStart(true); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && !dotBusy() && !uiFocusPreview().bad && uiFocusMode() !== 'dot'"
                title="The whole job runs with every burn at power 0: watch it trace"><i class="fas fa-eye"></i> Dry run</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { bridgeMode('off'); }, enable: canProbe() && bridge().mode" title="LightBurn can no longer move the head; the automatic mode waits until you pick a mode again"><i class="fas fa-stop"></i> Off</button>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-describe" data-bind="visible: bridge().mode, text: bridge().describe"></p>
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: dotMessage, visible: dotMessage"></p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> <span data-bind="text: obstaclesText"></span>
        Flat burns stop before the laser module (74 mm left, 40 mm right, 37 mm front and back of the beam) would come down over one.
      </p>
    </div>
    <!-- /ko -->

    <!-- rotary -->
    <!-- ko if: rotaryOn -->
    <div class="lhp-card" data-bind="visible: bridge().enabled">
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">1</span> The object</h5>
      <!-- ko if: rotary -->
      <p class="lhp-lead">
        <span data-bind="text: rotaryDiameterText"></span>
        <span class="text-warning" data-bind="visible: !rotary().complete"> (not complete: measure it on the Rotary tab)</span>
      </p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: rotary().diameter">
        In LightBurn's rotary setup use this diameter, and <code data-bind="text: 'dia=' + (rotary().diameter || 0).toFixed(2)"></code> in the device's start script.
      </p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <!-- ko ifnot: rotary -->
      <p class="text-warning">No rotary measurement yet: measure the object on the Rotary tab first.</p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">2</span> Rotary mode <span class="lhp-auto-note" data-bind="text: uiAutoNote"></span></h5>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: function () { bridgeMode('rotary'); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running()"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Rotary mode</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { bridgeMode('rotary', {dry_run: true}); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running()" title="Every burn goes out at power 0"><i class="fas fa-eye"></i> Dry run</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { bridgeMode('off'); }, enable: canProbe() && bridge().mode" title="LightBurn can no longer move the head; the automatic mode waits until you pick a mode again"><i class="fas fa-stop"></i> Off</button>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-describe" data-bind="visible: bridge().mode, text: bridge().describe"></p>
    </div>
    <!-- /ko -->

    <div class="lhp-card" data-bind="visible: bridge().enabled, css: {'lhp-card-danger': uiArmed}">
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">3</span> Laser</h5>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <!-- ko ifnot: uiArmed -->
        <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: uiArm, enable: !uiArmBlock(), css: {'lhp-arm-pending': uiArmPending}">
          <i class="fas fa-bolt"></i> <span data-bind="text: uiArmPending() ? 'Click again to arm' : 'Arm the laser'"></span>
        </button>
        <!-- /ko -->
        <!-- ko if: uiArmed -->
        <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: uiDisarm"><i class="fas fa-power-off"></i> Disarm</button>
        <!-- /ko -->
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { bridgePointer(true); }, enable: canProbe() && bridge().mode && !bridge().pointer"
                title="LightBurn's Fire button and laser-on framing: the 10W's beam capped low, or the 2W IR's crosshair"><i class="far fa-dot-circle"></i> Pointer on</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { bridgePointer(false); }, enable: canProbe() && bridge().pointer"><i class="far fa-circle"></i> Pointer off</button>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-preview text-warning" data-bind="visible: !uiArmed() && uiArmBlock(), text: uiArmBlock"></p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: !uiArmed() && !uiArmBlock()">Armed for 30 minutes at most. Opening the door disarms it.</p>
      <p class="lhp-msg text-error" data-bind="text: laserMessage, visible: laserMessage"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-wind"></i> Air purifier</h5>
      <p data-bind="text: purifierText"></p>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: purifierStop, enable: purifierInfo().power || (purifierInfo().phase && purifierInfo().phase !== 'idle')"><i class="fas fa-stop"></i> Stop the purifier</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: purifierTest, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && purifierInfo().phase === 'idle'" title="Socket on, gear 1 for 5 s, then off: checks the wiring">Test (5 s)</button>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: purifierMessage, visible: purifierMessage"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-history"></i> Recent burns</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: !burnRows().length">No burns yet.</p>
      <div class="lhp-burns" data-bind="foreach: burnRows">
        <div class="lhp-burn" data-bind="attr: {title: title}">
          <!-- ko if: src -->
          <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-bind="attr: {href: src}" title="Open the close-up of this burn">
            <img class="lhp-burn-thumb" alt="Close-up of the burn" data-bind="attr: {src: src}">
          </a>
          <!-- /ko -->
          <!-- ko ifnot: src -->
          <div class="lhp-burn-thumb lhp-burn-none" data-bind="attr: {title: rotary ? 'Rotary burns have no close-up photo' : 'No close-up photo'}"><i data-bind="css: rotary ? 'fas fa-sync-alt' : 'far fa-image'"></i></div>
          <!-- /ko -->
          <div class="lhp-small">
            <strong data-bind="text: when"></strong> <span data-bind="text: detail"></span><br>
            <span data-bind="text: status, css: {'text-warning': failed}"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-actions" data-bind="visible: burnRows().length">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: burnClear, enable: canProbe()"><i class="fas fa-trash"></i> Clear the list</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: !(burnHistory() || {}).enabled">The close-up after a burn is off (OctoBurn settings, Head camera and close-ups).</p>
      <p class="lhp-msg text-error" data-bind="text: burnMessage, visible: burnMessage"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================================================================== CAMERA -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('camera')">
    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-camera"></i> Close-up camera</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: closeupText"></p>
      <div class="lhp-closeup laserheightprobe-closeup">
        <img data-bind="attr: {src: closeupSrc}" alt="">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 350" preserveAspectRatio="none"
             data-bind="event: {mousedown: closeupDragStart, mousemove: closeupDragMove, mouseup: closeupDragEnd, mouseleave: closeupDragEnd}">
          <!-- ko if: closeupPlanData -->
          <rect fill="none" stroke="#e33" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="3,2"
                data-bind="attr: closeupRectAttr(closeupPlanData().sweep_lb)"></rect>
          <!-- ko foreach: closeupPlanData().tiles -->
          <rect fill="none" stroke="#3a3" stroke-width="0.5" data-bind="attr: $parent.closeupRectAttr(view_lb)"></rect>
          <!-- /ko -->
          <!-- /ko -->
          <!-- ko foreach: obstacles -->
          <rect fill="rgba(220,40,40,0.18)" stroke="#d33" stroke-width="0.6"
                data-bind="attr: $parent.closeupRectAttr(box)"></rect>
          <!-- /ko -->
          <!-- ko if: closeupBox -->
          <rect fill="rgba(255,255,0,0.15)" stroke="#ff0" stroke-width="0.8"
                data-bind="attr: closeupRectAttr([closeupBox().x0, closeupBox().y0, closeupBox().x1, closeupBox().y1])"></rect>
          <!-- /ko -->
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">Drag a box round the work. Yellow: your box. Dashed red: where the module will go. Red: obstacles.</p>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: closeupOverview, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running()"
                title="The 10W's whole-bed photo from Z290: the image the box is drawn on"><i class="fas fa-image"></i> Overview</button>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: closeupStart, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupBox()"><i class="fas fa-search-plus"></i> <span data-bind="text: closeupStartText"></span></button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: closeupPlan, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupBox()" title="Show the tiles and the module's sweep, without moving">Plan</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: closeupClear, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Clear</button>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-fields">
        <label>Height of the tallest thing under the dashed area <input type="number" step="0.1" min="0" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: closeupHeight"> mm</label>
        <label class="muted">Stand-off <input type="number" step="1" min="35" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: closeupStandoff"> mm</label>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: closeupMessage, visible: closeupMessage"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-ruler-vertical"></i> Measure the box</h5>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: dotMeasure, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupBox() && dotInfo().calibrated && !dotBusy()"
                title="The 10W's red autofocus light, photographed from two heights: the height of the surface at the box's centre (about 1 min, laser off)"><i class="far fa-dot-circle"></i> Height from the red dot</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: obstacleMark, enable: canProbe() && closeupBox()"
                title="Flat burns then keep the laser module off this box, if the object is taller than the module clears (uses the height above)"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> Mark as an obstacle</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: obstacleClear, enable: canProbe() && obstacles().length">Clear obstacles</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: dotText"></p>
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: dotMessage, visible: dotMessage"></p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: obstaclesText"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-video"></i> In LightBurn</h5>
      <p class="lhp-small">Add a network camera with this address, or use the "10W close-up" camera already set up:</p>
      <div class="lhp-url">
        <code data-bind="text: closeupUrl"></code>
        <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: uiCopyUrl"><i class="far fa-copy"></i> Copy</button>
        <span class="muted" data-bind="text: uiCopied"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================================================================== SURFACE -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('surface')">
    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-mountain"></i> Height map</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        A loaded map goes into the printer's own bed mesh, so every move, including LightBurn's, follows the surface.
        The map is zero at its lowest point: that is where the focus is set.
      </p>
      <div class="lhp-status-line" data-bind="visible: heightMap() || meshState().loaded">
        <span data-bind="visible: meshState().loaded"><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success"></i> <strong>Loaded in the printer</strong>, levelling on (<span data-bind="text: meshLoadedText"></span>).</span>
        <span data-bind="visible: !meshState().loaded"><i class="far fa-circle"></i> The printer has its print mesh.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: loadMap, enable: canProbe() && heightMap() && printerReady() && !running()"><i class="fas fa-upload"></i> Load into the printer</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: restoreMap, enable: canProbe() && meshState().loaded && printerReady() && !running()" title="Put the printer's own print mesh back (before 3D printing)">Restore print mesh</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: mapBed, visible: heightMap() && heightMap().source === 'red dot', enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && !dotBusy()"
                title="Put the last probed bed map back (loaded into the printer straight away if a map is loaded)"><i class="fas fa-undo"></i> Back to the bed map</button>
      </div>
      <div class="alert alert-error" data-bind="visible: meshState().warning, text: meshState().warning"></div>

      <!-- ko with: heightMap -->
      <table class="table table-condensed laserheightprobe-map-summary">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Made from</th><td data-bind="text: points + ' points' + (module ? ', ' + module : '') + (source === 'red dot' ? ' (red dot, an object)' : '')"></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Lowest point (focus here)</th>
              <td><strong data-bind="text: 'X' + base.x.toFixed(2) + ' Y' + base.y.toFixed(2)"></strong>
                  <span data-bind="text: base.focus === null || base.focus === undefined ? ' (calibrate the focus offset to get its focus Z)' : ', focus Z ' + base.focus.toFixed(3)"></span>
                  <div class="muted" data-bind="visible: base.machine_focus !== null && base.machine_focus !== undefined,
                       text: 'Machine focus Z ' + (base.machine_focus || 0).toFixed(3) + ': the number for the G53 G0 Z line in LightBurn\'s start G-code (check this on the machine first).'"></div></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Height range</th><td data-bind="text: range.toFixed(2) + ' mm, steepest ' + slope_deg + '°'"></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Fit</th><td data-bind="text: 'worst miss ' + (worst.miss >= 0 ? '+' : '') + worst.miss.toFixed(3) + ' mm at X' + worst.x.toFixed(1) + ' Y' + worst.y.toFixed(1) + ', rms ' + rms.toFixed(3) + ' mm (tolerance ' + tolerance + ')'"></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <!-- ko foreach: warnings -->
      <div class="alert" data-bind="text: $data"></div>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <div class="lhp-mesh-wrap">
        <table class="laserheightprobe-mesh">
          <tbody data-bind="foreach: $parent.meshRows">
            <tr data-bind="foreach: $data">
              <td data-bind="text: text, style: {backgroundColor: colour}, attr: {title: title}"></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="muted lhp-small">The printer's mesh, back row at the top, in mm above the lowest point.</p>
      </div>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <!-- ko ifnot: heightMap -->
      <p class="muted">No height map yet. Make one from the red dot (below) or from a probe job (Probe tab).</p>
      <!-- /ko -->
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="far fa-dot-circle"></i> Make a map</h5>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: dotMap, enable: uiHasCamera() && canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupBox() && dotInfo().calibrated && !dotBusy()"
                title="No probe swap: one red-dot reading per point over the box drawn on the Camera tab (about 12 s a point, laser off). Records the object as an obstacle, and loads straight away if a map is loaded.">With the red dot</button>
        <label class="lhp-inline">every <input type="number" min="10" max="100" step="5" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: dotMapStep"> mm over the box on the Camera tab</label>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: buildMap, enable: canProbe() && rows().length && !running()">From the probe results</button>
        <span class="muted lhp-small">Run a grid of points on the Probe tab first.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================================================================== ROTARY -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('rotary')">
    <!-- ko if: rotaryOn -->
    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-sync-alt"></i> The object in the chuck</h5>
      <!-- ko if: rotary -->
      <p class="lhp-lead">
        <span data-bind="text: rotaryDiameterText"></span><span data-bind="visible: rotary().body_length, text: rotary().body_length ? ', body Y' + rotary().body_from_y + ' to Y' + rotary().body_to_y + ' (' + rotary().body_length.toFixed(1) + ' mm)' : ''"></span>
        <span class="text-warning" data-bind="visible: !rotary().complete">, not complete</span>
      </p>
      <p data-bind="visible: rotaryRunoutText, css: {'text-warning': rotary().runout_within === false}, text: rotaryRunoutText"
         title="How far the top rises and falls as the rotary turns. Rotary mode follows it in Z."></p>
      <!-- ko foreach: uiRotaryState -->
      <p class="lhp-small" data-bind="text: text, css: tone"></p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: uiRotaryHousing, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && sessionOk() && rotary().complete !== undefined"
                title="Two touches on the rotary's housing (about a minute, probe on). If it moved sideways, the measurement is marked stale."><i class="fas fa-question-circle"></i> Has the rotary moved?</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: uiRotaryVerify, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && sessionOk() && rotary().complete && !rotary().stale"
                title="Touch the top where the measurement says it is, at 4 positions and 4 angles, and beside the crest (about 10 minutes, probe on)"><i class="fas fa-check-double"></i> Verify against the object</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: downloadTemplate"><i class="fas fa-download"></i> LightBurn template</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: !sessionOk()">The probe buttons need a tap test this session (Control tab panel).</p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <!-- ko ifnot: rotary -->
      <p class="muted">Not measured yet.</p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: uiRotaryCheck, visible: uiRotaryCheck"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">1</span> Measure with the probe</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        Touches the rotary's housing, the object at four turns near each end, fits the axis and finds the body's ends.
        Measure again starts from the last measurement (and follows the housing if the rotary moved). A new object starts
        from a Probe here on its top. The ends below are guesses: it finds the real ones.
      </p>
      <p class="lhp-small" data-bind="css: {'text-warning': uiHomedHead() !== 'laser', 'text-success': uiHomedHead() === 'laser'}">
        <i class="fas" data-bind="css: uiHomedHead() === 'laser' ? 'fa-check-circle' : 'fa-exclamation-triangle'"></i>
        <span data-bind="text: uiHomedHeadText"></span>
      </p>
      <div class="lhp-fields">
        <label>Free end about Y <input type="number" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: rotaryFrom, enable: !running()" title="A guess: where the object's free end is"></label>
        <label>body ends near the chuck about Y <input type="number" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: rotaryTo, enable: !running()" title="A guess: where the full diameter stops before the shoulder or neck"></label>
        <label>never past Y <input type="number" class="input-mini" placeholder="body" data-bind="value: rotaryChuckLimit, enable: !running()" title="Blank: the rotary body (the head never passes Y293.4). Objects can sit over the chuck."></label>
        <label>known diameter <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: rotaryKnown, enable: !running()" title="Only to calibrate the housing reference on an object you have calipered"> mm</label>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: uiRotaryRemeasure, visible: rotary() && rotary().axis_x != null, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && sessionOk()"
                title="Starts from the last measurement, and follows the housing if the rotary has moved: no Probe here needed"><i class="fas fa-redo"></i> Measure again</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: measureRotary, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && sessionOk(), css: {'btn-primary': !(rotary() && rotary().axis_x != null)}"
                title="A new object: starts from your last Probe here on its top"><i class="fas fa-ruler-combined"></i> Measure a new object</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: uiRotaryResume, visible: rotary() && rotary().partial, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && sessionOk()">Resume</button>
        <span class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: !sessionOk()">Needs a tap test this session (Control tab panel).</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><span class="lhp-step">2</span> Check with the red dot</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">With the 10W on (the red dot is the 10W's), no probe swap: reads the top at six points from high above and compares with the measurement. Height only: it cannot see the object shifted sideways.</p>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: uiRotaryDotCheck, enable: uiHasCamera() && canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && !dotBusy() && dotInfo().calibrated && rotary() && rotary().complete"><i class="far fa-dot-circle"></i> Check the height</button>
      </div>
      <p class="lhp-msg" data-bind="text: uiRotaryCheck, visible: uiRotaryCheck"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-redo"></i> Turn the rotary</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">The pin stows and the head goes up before the rotary turns. For levelling with a spirit level, or looking round the object.</p>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { rotaryTurn({by: -90}); }, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()">&minus;90&deg;</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { rotaryTurn({by: 90}); }, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()">+90&deg;</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { rotaryTurn({to: 0}); }, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()">Back to B0</button>
        <span data-bind="text: rotaryTurnText"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- /ko -->
  </div>

  <!-- ===================================================================== PROBE -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('probe')">
    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Measure points</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        For one spot, use the <strong>OctoBurn probe</strong> panel in the Control tab (jog the pin over it, Probe here).
        This measures a list of points in one job.
      </p>
      <!-- ko ifnot: running -->
      <label class="checkbox" data-bind="visible: canProbe">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: setupConfirmed">
        The probe head is in the bay, the laser is parked beam-down on something that cannot burn, and safe Z clears the object everywhere with the pin out.
      </label>
      <p class="text-error" data-bind="text: readyText, visible: readyText"></p>
      <p class="text-error" data-bind="visible: !tapTestEnabled()">
        The tap test is off in the settings, so nothing proves a touch reaches the probe board today.
      </p>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: start, enable: canStart, visible: canProbe"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Measure the points</button>
        <span class="muted lhp-small">Each job starts with a tap test.</span>
      </div>
      <!-- /ko -->
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5>Points</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        One laser position per line, "X Y" in printer coordinates. Add <code>ref</code> to the bed or reference point, and
        <code>datum</code> to the point LightBurn's Z offsets count from (the first point if none).
      </p>
      <textarea rows="6" class="input-block-level laserheightprobe-points" data-bind="value: pointsText, enable: canProbe"></textarea>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: savePoints, enable: canProbe">Save points</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: addPosition, enable: canProbe() && !running()"
                title="Reads M114 and adds where the pin is now: head position plus the probe XY offset">Add current position</button>
      </div>
      <form class="form-inline laserheightprobe-grid lhp-fields" data-bind="submit: makeGrid">
        Grid from X <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridX0">
        Y <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridY0">
        to X <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridX1">
        Y <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridY1">,
        <input type="number" step="1" min="1" max="20" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridNx"> by
        <input type="number" step="1" min="1" max="20" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: gridNy"> points
        <button class="btn btn-small" type="submit" data-bind="enable: canProbe">Replace the list</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5>Results</h5>
      <!-- ko ifnot: rows().length -->
      <p class="muted">No job has finished yet.</p>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <!-- ko if: rows().length -->
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: resultCaption"></p>
      <div class="lhp-table-wrap">
        <table class="table table-condensed laserheightprobe-results">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>#</th><th>X</th><th>Y</th><th>Trigger Z</th><th>Height above ref</th>
                <th>Focus Z</th><th>LightBurn Z offset</th><th>Datum</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody data-bind="foreach: rows">
            <!-- ko if: failed -->
            <tr><td data-bind="text: index + 1"></td><td colspan="7" class="text-error">failed</td></tr>
            <!-- /ko -->
            <!-- ko ifnot: failed -->
            <tr data-bind="css: {info: is_datum}">
              <td data-bind="text: (index + 1) + (is_reference ? ' ref' : '')"></td>
              <td data-bind="text: x.toFixed(2)"></td>
              <td data-bind="text: y.toFixed(2)"></td>
              <td><span data-bind="text: z.toFixed(3)"></span>
                  <span class="muted" data-bind="text: 'spread ' + spread.toFixed(3) + ', n=' + n + (taken !== n ? ' of ' + taken : '')"></span></td>
              <td data-bind="text: $parent.num(height, true)"></td>
              <td data-bind="text: $parent.num(focus, false)"></td>
              <td><strong data-bind="text: $parent.num(lightburn, true)"></strong></td>
              <td><input type="radio" name="laserheightprobe_datum" data-bind="checked: $parent.datumText, value: String(index)"></td>
            </tr>
            <!-- /ko -->
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="alert laserheightprobe-sign lhp-small">
        <strong>Check the sign once.</strong> The LightBurn Z offset is focus at the point minus focus at the datum, so positive
        means that point's focus is higher. Give a test layer +1 mm in LightBurn, run it with the beam off and watch Z: if the
        head goes down, tick "Flip the sign" in the plugin settings.
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: copyText"><i class="far fa-copy"></i> Copy as text</button>
        <span class="muted" data-bind="text: copyMessage"></span>
      </div>
      <!-- /ko -->
      <textarea readonly rows="6" id="laserheightprobe_text" class="input-block-level laserheightprobe-text" data-bind="value: tableText, visible: rows().length"></textarea>
    </div>

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5>Heights</h5>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        From your machine, no defaults. Safe Z: where the pin, deployed, clears the whole object. Z floor: just above the bed or
        fixture. No probing step goes below the floor.
      </p>
      <div class="lhp-fields">
        <label>Safe Z <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: safeZInput, enable: canProbe() && !running()"></label>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { captureHeight('safe_z'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Use current Z</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { saveHeight('safe_z', safeZInput()); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Save</button>
      </div>
      <div class="lhp-fields">
        <label>Z floor <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: zFloorInput, enable: canProbe() && !running()"></label>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { captureHeight('z_floor'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Use current Z</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { saveHeight('z_floor', zFloorInput()); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Save</button>
      </div>
      <p class="text-error" data-bind="text: heightsText, visible: heightsText"></p>
    </div>

    <details class="lhp-card lhp-details">
      <summary><i class="fas fa-tools"></i> Probe hardware</summary>
      <p class="lhp-small">
        Board at <code data-bind="text: espUrl"></code>.
        Latched: <strong data-bind="text: yesNo(probeStatus().latched)"></strong>,
        output: <strong data-bind="text: probeStatus().raw === true ? 'HIGH' : (probeStatus().raw === false ? 'LOW' : '?')"></strong>,
        triggers since boot: <strong data-bind="text: probeStatus().trigger_count === undefined || probeStatus().trigger_count === null ? '?' : probeStatus().trigger_count"></strong>
        <span class="text-error" data-bind="text: probeStatus().error"></span>
      </p>
      <div class="btn-group laserheightprobe-buttons">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: readProbe">Read</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('deploy'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Deploy</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('stow'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Stow</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('reset'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Reset alarm</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: checkWiring, enable: canProbe() && !running() && !checking()">Test the wiring</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        The wiring test puts the probe in touch mode, pin up, and expects HIGH. Some BLTouch clones have no touch mode, so a
        failure there is not proof of a fault: deploy the pin, push it up by hand and press Read.
        <strong data-bind="text: checkResult"></strong>
      </p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: setOdMode, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Set the probe to open-drain</button>
        One-off, stored in the probe. Only if a meter shows 5 V on the white wire (it goes straight to GPIO3).
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================================================================== CALIBRATE -->
  <div class="lhp-pane" data-bind="visible: uiShow('setup')">

    <div class="lhp-card">
      <h5><i class="fas fa-microchip"></i> Laser module</h5>
      <p>
        <!-- ko if: pickModule -->
        <select data-bind="options: modules, optionsText: moduleLabel, optionsValue: 'name', value: selectedModule, enable: canProbe() && !running()" title="M1006 cannot name this laser: pick it"></select>
        <!-- /ko -->
        <!-- ko ifnot: pickModule -->
        <strong data-bind="text: selectedModule"></strong> <span class="muted">(from M1006)</span>
        <!-- /ko -->
        <span class="muted" data-bind="text: selectedOffsetText"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: detectedText"></p>
      <div class="lhp-fields">
        Probe XY offset (pin minus beam): dx
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: dxInput, enable: canProbe() && !running()">
        dy <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: dyInput, enable: canProbe() && !running()">
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: saveXy, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Save</button>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: clearXy, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Clear</button>
      </div>
      <p class="text-warning lhp-small" data-bind="visible: xyMissing">
        This module's beam position relative to the pin is not measured, so the pin touches where the 10W's beam would be (0, 0).
      </p>
    </div>

    <details class="lhp-card lhp-details">
      <summary><i class="fas fa-bullseye"></i> Focus offset <span class="muted" data-bind="text: selectedOffsetText"></span></summary>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">
        Focus Z = trigger Z + the module's focus offset. The LightBurn column does not need it: the offset cancels out of the differences.
      </p>
      <ol class="laserheightprobe-steps">
        <li>
          With the probe head in the bay, probe a flat reference spot.
          X <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: calibX">
          Y <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: calibY">
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: calibrateProbe, enable: canStart">Probe the reference spot</button>
          <div class="muted lhp-small">Tick the setup box on the Probe tab first; this also starts with a tap test. Or Probe here over the spot in the Control tab, then
            <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: useHereReference, enable: canProbe() && hereRows().length">Use the last Probe here result</button>
          </div>
          <div class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="text: calibrationText"></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          Swap the laser in (no power cycle: it stayed plugged in). Jog it over the same spot to best focus with the beam off:
          <div class="lhp-fields">
            Laser focus Z <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: laserFocusZ">
            <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: useCurrentZ, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Use current Z</button>
            <button class="btn btn-small btn-primary" data-bind="click: saveFromFocus, enable: canProbe() && hasReference()">Save offset</button>
          </div>
          <div class="lhp-fields">
            Or the card method, a card under the hood just drags at Z <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: touchZ">
            <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: useCurrentTouchZ, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Use current Z</button>
            card <input type="number" step="any" min="0" max="2" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: cardThickness" placeholder="mm">
            + focal distance <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: focalDistance">
            <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: saveFromTouch, enable: canProbe() && hasReference()">Save offset</button>
          </div>
          <div class="muted lhp-small">The card lifts the hood by its own thickness (0 if the hood touches the bare surface). Focal distance: 10 for the 10W.</div>
          <div class="lhp-small" data-bind="text: touchPreview, css: {'text-error': touchPreviewWarning, muted: !touchPreviewWarning()}"></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          Swap the probe head back and Probe here over the same spot again. A Z lost in the swap shows here:
          <div class="lhp-small" data-bind="text: retouchText, css: {'text-error': retouchBad}"></div>
          <div class="muted lhp-small" data-bind="visible: swapText, text: swapText"></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          Or type it: <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: typedOffset">
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: saveTyped, enable: canProbe">Save offset</button>
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: clearOffset, enable: canProbe">Clear</button>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p data-bind="text: offsetMessage, css: {'text-error': offsetWarning}"></p>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">Confirm the offset on material with a focus ladder (README, "Calibration checks"). It burns, so it is a file you check and run yourself, never a button here.</p>
    </details>

    <!-- ko ifnot: rotaryOn -->
    <details class="lhp-card lhp-details laserheightprobe-calib" data-bind="visible: uiHasCamera">
      <summary><i class="fas fa-camera"></i> Close-up camera and red dot <span class="muted" data-bind="text: closeupCalibText"></span></summary>
      <p class="muted lhp-small">Only needed once, or after the camera or the module is knocked. Each step uses the newest photos; nothing is used until the last button.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="plugin/laserheightprobe/closeup_board.png" target="_blank">Print the board</a> on A4 at 100 % (no scaling) and tape it flat in the middle of the bare bed.</li>
        <li><label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: closeupCalibClear">
          The bed holds nothing but the board (or the crosses' paper): the head goes down to Z40.</label>
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { closeupCalibCapture('board'); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupCalibClear()">Photograph the board (about 25 min)</button>
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: closeupCalibSolve, enable: canProbe() && !running() && closeupCalibInfo().board">Solve the lens</button></li>
        <li>Take the board off. Burn the four alignment crosses (16 mm, at LightBurn (60, 100), (200, 100), (60, 250), (200, 250)) on
          fresh paper, and photograph them before anything moves:
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { closeupCalibCapture('cross'); }, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupCalibClear()">Photograph the crosses (about 7 min)</button>
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: closeupCalibTie, enable: canProbe() && !running() && closeupCalibInfo().cross && closeupCalibInfo().candidate">Tie to the beam</button></li>
        <li>For the red dot: draw a box on flat paper on the Camera tab with nothing tall to its right (the dot's light comes in from
          the right), tick the box above, then
          <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: dotCalibrate, enable: canProbe() && printerReady() && !running() && closeupBox() && closeupCalibClear() && !dotBusy()">Calibrate the red dot there (about 3 min)</button></li>
        <li><button class="btn btn-small btn-primary" data-bind="click: closeupCalibAccept, enable: canProbe() && !running() && closeupCalibReady()">Use this calibration</button></li>
      </ol>
      <p data-bind="text: closeupCalibMessage, visible: closeupCalibMessage"></p>
    </details>
    <!-- /ko -->
  </div>

  <!-- the log drawer -->
  <div class="lhp-log-drawer">
    <a href="#" class="lhp-log-toggle" data-bind="click: function () { uiLogOpen(!uiLogOpen()); }">
      <i class="fas" data-bind="css: uiLogOpen() ? 'fa-chevron-down' : 'fa-chevron-right'"></i> Activity log
    </a>
    <pre id="laserheightprobe_log" class="laserheightprobe-log" data-bind="text: log, visible: uiLogOpen"></pre>
  </div>
</div>
